{
  "question": "How do I start a PA for a non-preferred drug for an NY Medicaid pt: who do I contact and what form?",
  "status": "answered",
  "assumption": "Assuming NY Medicaid FFS (NYRx), as stated in the question.",
  "answer": "Assuming NY Medicaid FFS (NYRx): only the prescriber or their authorized agent can submit the PA. You can't submit it as a third party, but you can start it.\n\n1. **Pharmacy-initiated ePA:** If you use CoverMyMeds, start the ePA there. It routes to the prescriber's queue, and the prescriber completes and submits it to NYRx.\n2. **Prescriber options:**\n   - CoverMyMeds ePA.\n   - PAXpress (web, via eMedNY).\n   - The NYRx Clinical Call Center at 1-877-309-9493.\n   - The PA fax form at newyork.fhsc.com/providers/PA_forms.asp.\n3. **Questions:** Call NYRx Education & Outreach at 1-833-967-7310 or email NYRxEO@primetherapeutics.com.\n4. **Emergency supply:** If you can't reach the prescriber, you may obtain a PA for up to a 72-hour emergency supply.",
